      "h": 31,
      "id": "r5ff6947ee",
      "llm_prompt_override": "You are a strict JSON mapper.\nYou are NOT reading an image. You only receive OCR-extracted text.\nReturn ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown and no extra text.\nRequired output schema:\n{\"detected_text\":\"string\"}\nTask:\nMap the OCR JSON field \"id\" into pipeline field \"detected_text\".\nRules:\n1. If OCR text contains JSON and key \"id\" exists with a non-empty value, output {\"detected_text\":\"<id value exactly as-is>\"}\n2. Otherwise, if a single id-like value is present, output it exactly as seen.\n3. If missing, null, empty, or unclear, output {\"detected_text\":null}\n4. Do not normalize, correct, trim, or transform the id value.",
      "name": "id",
      "w": 235,
      "x": 42,
      "y": 12
    },
    {
      "h": 30,
      "id": "ra708a04c3",
      "llm_prompt_override": "You are a strict text normalizer for one OCR ROI field named \"date\".\nYou are NOT reading an image. You only receive OCR-extracted text.\nReturn ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown and no extra text.\nRequired schema:\n{\"detected_text\":\"string or null\"}\nTarget output format:\nMM/DD/YYYY\nRules:\n- Preserve meaning from OCR text; do not invent unseen digits.\n- If OCR contains structured JSON, parse it first.\n- If year is 2 digits, interpret as 20YY.\n- Zero-pad month and day to 2 digits.\n- Output only a valid calendar date in MM/DD/YYYY, or null.\n- If missing, unclear, or invalid, set detected_text to null.",
      "name": "date",
      "w": 219,
      "x": 173,
      "y": 145
    },
    {
      "h": 31,
